{% set local_problem %}
<p>Athens' mature tree coverage is one of the city's best features — and one of its biggest gutter challenges. The historic areas around Athens Square feature century-old oaks that drop massive amounts of leaves every fall. Pine trees throughout Limestone County shed needles constantly. The neighborhoods near Athens State University have dense canopy coverage that keeps gutters perpetually filling.</p>

<p>For many Athens homeowners, gutter cleaning becomes a recurring burden. Professional cleaning costs $150-200 per visit, and most homes need it 3-4 times per year. That's $600-800 annually — more than a quality gutter guard system would cost over time.</p>

<p>The bigger risk is what happens between cleanings. When gutters clog during Athens' heavy storms, water overflows toward your foundation instead of away from it. This can cause basement flooding, crawlspace moisture, foundation damage, and landscape erosion.</p>

<p>Gutter guards solve this permanently. The right system keeps debris out while allowing water to flow freely. Install once, and the cleaning headache — and the overflow risk — is over.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Gutter guards are protective covers that fit over or inside your gutters, allowing water to flow through while blocking leaves, pine needles, twigs, and other debris. Different types work better for different debris challenges.</p>

<p>Micro-mesh guards with tiny perforations excel at blocking fine debris like pine needles — essential for many Athens properties. Screen guards handle larger oak and maple leaves effectively. Solid covers use surface tension to pull water into the gutter while debris slides off.</p>

<p>For most Athens homes, we recommend micro-mesh guards. They handle both fine and coarse debris, work well with the area's mix of pine and hardwood trees, and are tough enough to withstand heavy debris loads during storms. We'll assess your specific situation and recommend the right solution.</p>
{% endset %}

